{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/cloudfilesystemsetup\/setlocalstoredirectory(_:discardingexistingcache:)"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CloudFileSystemSetup"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setLocalStoreDirectory"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"path"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"discardingExistingCache"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"path","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event store’s directory, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when no store is available."}]}]},{"name":"discardingExistingCache","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", any cache already present for this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory must be deleted rather than loaded, and the backend must behave as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though it had never cached anything. The ensemble passes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" whenever the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store is being rebuilt, so a device starting over is guaranteed a full fetch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than a delta against a cursor from a previous incarnation."}]}]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CustomCloudBackends"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backends that cache remote state between launches should store that cache inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this directory. Doing so ties the cache’s lifetime to the event store’s: when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store is removed or rebuilt, the stale cache goes with it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caching remote state anywhere with an independent lifetime (the system caches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directory, for instance) is unsafe. Such a cache can outlive the event store it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"describes — surviving even app deletion — and a backend that then resumes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incremental fetch against a rebuilt cloud may never be told about files that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"predate its stale cursor. The device sees a partial cloud and reports no error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Called before priming, whenever the ensemble knows its event store. It is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called for ensemble-independent operations such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/retrieveEnsembleIdentifiers(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", so implementations must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tolerate priming without it and simply forgo persistent caching in that case."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","defaultImplementationsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc: